WEBVTT

NOTE Synthetic test material. All people, institutions, venues and results are fictional.

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Quillwave is a fictional project, made as synthetic test material.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.900
The task: recover a full 256x256 ripple field from only 64 point sensors.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.800
Simple interpolation blurs the wave fronts between the sensors.

4
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.900
Quillwave encodes the sensor readings into a compact latent field code.

5
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.800
A field decoder then predicts a value and a confidence at every pixel.

6
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.900
Left: linear interpolation of the sensors. Right: Quillwave.

7
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.800
The wave fronts stay sharp as the sources move.

8
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.600
On RippleBench-Synthetic, Quillwave reaches 29.46 dB PSNR.

9
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.800
That is 5.41 dB above radial-basis interpolation.

10
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.900
Limitations: all results are on synthetic fields only.

11
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.800
The baselines are not compute-matched, and the confidence map is not calibrated.
